insert into public.quick_reference_sections (id,body,version)
values ('beta-blocker-bolus','| Medication | Adult IV dose · pertinent details |
|---|---|
| **Esmolol (Brevibloc)** | **Gradual control: 500 mcg/kg (0.5 mg/kg) over 1 min**, then infusion as needed. **Immediate perioperative control: 1 mg/kg over 30 sec**, then **150 mcg/kg/min** if needed. Choose by urgency and hemodynamic tolerance; these are alternative regimens. Elimination half-life approximately **9 min**, not a guaranteed recovery time. ([FDA label](https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/019386s053lbl.pdf)) |
| **Metoprolol tartrate (Lopressor)** | **Stable AF rate control: 2.5–5 mg over 2 min**, up to **3 doses (maximum 15 mg)**; reassess BP/HR before each dose. ([AF guideline](https://www.ahajournals.org/doi/10.1161/CIR.0000000000001193)) This is **off-label in the US**; the US injection label is for hemodynamically stable acute MI. Half-life **3–7 h**: not rapidly reversible. Use **tartrate**, not oral extended-release succinate. ([US label](https://labeling.pfizer.com/ShowLabeling.aspx?id=17205)) |
| **Labetalol** | **Perioperative small bolus: 2.5–10 mg over 2 min**, individualized anesthesia practice. ([Perioperative review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6148691/)) **Separate severe-hypertension label regimen:** **20 mg over 2 min**, then **40–80 mg every 10 min** as needed; **300 mg cumulative maximum**. Peak BP effect usually within **5 min** of each injection. Avoid asthma, severe bradycardia, greater-than-first-degree block, overt HF and cardiogenic shock. ([Label](https://labeling.pfizer.com/ShowLabeling.aspx?id=4492)) |
| **Propranolol (Inderal)** | **AF guideline regimen: 1 mg over 1 min**, repeat every **2 min** as needed, up to **3 doses (3 mg)**. ([AF guideline](https://www.ahajournals.org/doi/10.1161/CIR.0000000000001193)) Nonselective beta blockade; **contraindicated in asthma, sinus bradycardia, greater-than-first-degree block and cardiogenic shock**. Use cautiously with anesthesia-related myocardial depression. **Do not use for pre-excited AF**; other accessory-pathway rhythms require rhythm-specific assessment, not a blanket WPW rule. See safety chart and WPW Syndrome. ([Label](https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=f14ea537-dd5c-4c78-9037-9a85e9e610ef); [AF guideline](https://www.ahajournals.org/doi/10.1161/CIR.0000000000001193)) |','2026-09-27-audit1')
on conflict (id) do update set body=excluded.body,version=excluded.version,updated_at=now();

